  "B_expression": "-1/(2*(1+sqrt(1+r))**2)",
  "C_expression": "0",
  "derivation": "This is the source-only construction inherited from the prior R4 finite-root work. With g = r/2 + r^2*B (C=0), the pure remainder 2g+g^2-r vanishes identically on the inner r-interval when u=0. Verification: setting s=sqrt(1+r), one checks that r^2*B = (s-1-r/2) exactly, so 2g+g^2-r = 2(r/2 + s-1-r/2) + (s-1)^2 - r = 2(s-1) + (s-1)^2 - (s^2-1) = 0. The expression is smooth for r > -1; the outer rectangle has |r| < 1/2 (smooth transition to 0 at |r|=1/2), so 1+r > 1/2 > 0 throughout the evaluation domain. No singularities, no branch cuts. C=0 means no u-correction is added; the whole residual E still carries the 2*u*g cross term for u!=0, which this construction does not address. All twelve displayed initial-feedback points have u=0, so the B correction is the only term that can reduce the observed residuals r^2/4.",
  "inspect": [
    {
      "file_id": "MATH/METHOD_GUIDE.md",
      "limit": 2048,
      "offset": 0
    }
  ]
  ,
  "note": "Successor should verify: (1) the sqrt(1+r) argument stays positive across the full outer rectangle including smooth-transition regions; (2) at u=0 the pure remainder is exactly zero, but the whole residual E = 2*u*g + (2g+g^2-r) still has the cross term for u!=0; (3) the LEFT family point with r=-1.0 falls outside chi_r support so the body is never evaluated there; (4) C=0 is a deliberate choice, not an absence of action -- a future stage may add a C term to address the u-dependent cross term if the field develops nonzero u values; (5) this expression is a coefficient-field operator for the two-slot covariance quotient, not a full PDE solution."
